---
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <!-- Subtle background gradient -->
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-amber-50/60 via-transparent to-transparent pointer-events-none"></div>

  <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-20 md:pt-24 md:pb-28">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <!-- Badge -->
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-100/80 border border-amber-200/60 mb-8">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-amber-800 tracking-wide">AI-Powered Patent Prosecution</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Headline -->
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-stone-900 tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-6">
        Respond to Office Actions
        <span class="text-amber-600"> in minutes,</span>
        <br class="hidden sm:block" />
        not days
      </h1>

      <!-- Subtitle -->
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
        Upload your Office Action and let AI analyze every rejection, read the cited prior art, and recommend argue-or-amend strategies with confidence scores — so you can focus on the prosecution decisions that matter.
      </p>

      <!-- CTAs -->
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 mb-4">
        <a
          href="/agent"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 text-base font-medium text-white bg-amber-600 hover:bg-amber-700 rounded-lg transition-colors shadow-sm"
        >
          Start Analyzing Free
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#how-it-works"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 text-base font-medium text-stone-700 bg-white hover:bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-lg transition-colors"
        >
          See How It Works
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-400">No credit card required. Analyze your first Office Action free.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Realistic product mock: fake agent conversation -->
    <div class="mt-16 md:mt-20 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="relative rounded-xl border border-stone-200/80 bg-white shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
        <!-- App chrome bar -->
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 bg-stone-50 border-b border-stone-100">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <div class="flex gap-1.5">
              <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-stone-200"></div>
              <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-stone-200"></div>
              <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-stone-200"></div>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-stone-400">Solve This OA For Me</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="px-2 py-1 rounded bg-stone-100 text-[10px] text-stone-400 font-medium">Session #1847</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Fake chat conversation -->
        <div class="p-5 md:p-6 space-y-5 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-stone-50/30" style="max-height: 480px; overflow: hidden;">

          <!-- User message: upload -->
          <div class="flex justify-end">
            <div class="max-w-md bg-stone-100 rounded-2xl rounded-tr-sm px-4 py-3">
              <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">I received a §103 rejection on claims 1-12. The examiner is combining Smith (US 10,234,567) and Jones (US 2021/0045678). Here's the Office Action and my application.</p>
              <div class="flex gap-2 mt-2.5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-stone-200 text-xs text-stone-500">
                  <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="text-red-400"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                  OA_2024-0892.pdf
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-stone-200 text-xs text-stone-500">
                  <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="text-red-400"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                  App_16-789012.pdf
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Agent message: analysis -->
          <div class="flex justify-start">
            <div class="max-w-lg space-y-3">
              <!-- Tool card: reading OA -->
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-100 rounded-lg text-xs text-amber-700">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="text-amber-500"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                <span class="font-medium">Reading</span> OA_2024-0892.pdf <span class="text-amber-400">&middot; pages 1-14</span>
              </div>

              <!-- Tool card: reading prior art -->
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-100 rounded-lg text-xs text-amber-700">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="text-amber-500"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"/><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"/></svg>
                <span class="font-medium">Analyzing</span> Smith (US 10,234,567) <span class="text-amber-400">&middot; col. 4-7</span>
              </div>

              <!-- Agent text response -->
              <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl rounded-tl-sm border border-stone-100 px-4 py-3 shadow-sm">
                <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">I've analyzed the Office Action. Here's what I found:</p>

                <div class="space-y-3">
                  <!-- Rejection summary -->
                  <div class="p-3 bg-stone-50 rounded-lg border border-stone-100">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-700">§103 Rejection — Claims 1-5</span>
                      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium text-amber-600 bg-amber-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Recommend: Argue</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Smith discloses a "multi-layer authentication module" (col. 5, ll. 12-34) but does not teach the claimed <em>dynamic threshold adjustment</em>. The examiner relies on Jones ¶[0067] for this element, but Jones describes a static threshold in a different context (batch processing, not real-time). <strong>Confidence: 82%</strong></p>
                  </div>

                  <div class="p-3 bg-stone-50 rounded-lg border border-stone-100">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-700">§103 Rejection — Claims 6-12</span>
                      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium text-stone-600 bg-stone-100 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Recommend: Amend</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">The combination of Smith and Jones does fairly teach the "data aggregation pipeline" of claim 6. However, amending to incorporate the "priority queue with weighted scoring" from dependent claim 9 would distinguish over both references. <strong>Confidence: 91%</strong></p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Fade overlay at bottom -->
          <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-16 bg-gradient-to-t from-white to-transparent pointer-events-none"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
